{"findings": [
{"file": "themes/src/main/resources-community/theme/base/account/messages/messages_lt.properties", "line": 101, "severity": "medium", "category": "doc_defect", "title": "Lithuanian totpStep1 replaced with Italian text", "body": "The Lithuanian `totpStep1` value was replaced with \"Installa una delle seguenti applicazioni sul tuo cellulare:\", which is Italian. Lithuanian users of the account theme will see an Italian sentence. It should be a Lithuanian translation, or the key should be removed so it falls back to English."},
{"file": "themes/src/main/resources-community/theme/base/login/messages/messages_lt.properties", "line": 71, "severity": "medium", "category": "doc_defect", "title": "Lithuanian loginTotpStep1 replaced with Italian text", "body": "`loginTotpStep1` in the Lithuanian login bundle now reads \"Installa una delle seguenti applicazioni sul tuo cellulare:\", which is Italian. Lithuanian users will see an Italian instruction on the OTP setup page. Use a Lithuanian string, or drop the key so the English fallback is used."},
{"file": "themes/src/main/resources-community/theme/base/account/messages/messages_zh_CN.properties", "line": 112, "severity": "low", "category": "doc_defect", "title": "Simplified Chinese bundle gets Traditional Chinese text", "body": "The new zh_CN `totpStep1` value \"在您的手機上安裝以下應用程式之一：\" is written in Traditional Chinese characters (zh_TW style). The rest of the file uses Simplified Chinese, so users will see mixed scripts. It should be something like \"在您的手机上安装以下应用之一：\"."},
{"file": "js/apps/account-ui/maven-resources/theme/keycloak.v3/account/messages/messages_en.properties", "line": 188, "severity": "medium", "category": "bug", "title": "Java MessageFormat syntax introduced into i18next-based bundle", "body": "This bundle uses i18next interpolation (`{{0}}`, `{{name}}`), as every other key in the file does. The new `error-invalid-multivalued-size` value uses Java MessageFormat placeholders (`{0}`) and a ChoiceFormat expression (`{2,choice,0#values|1#value|1<values}`). i18next will not substitute these, so the account console will show the raw placeholder text to users. Keep the `{{n}}` syntax and use i18next pluralization instead. The same problem applies to the identical change in `js/apps/admin-ui/maven-resources/theme/keycloak.v2/admin/messages/messages_en.properties`."},
{"file": "misc/theme-verifier/src/main/java/org/keycloak/themeverifier/VerifyMessageProperties.java", "line": 157, "severity": "low", "category": "bug", "title": "Anchor mismatch message lacks key and file", "body": "The \"Didn't find anchor tag ...\" message does not say which key or file is affected, unlike the duplicate-key and Illegal HTML messages. When the verifier runs over hundreds of bundles, maintainers cannot locate the offending translation. Include `key` and `file` in the message."},
{"file": "misc/theme-verifier/src/main/java/org/keycloak/themeverifier/VerifyMessageProperties.java", "line": 145, "severity": "low", "category": "bug", "title": "ANCHOR_PATTERN matches any tag starting with 'a'", "body": "`</?a[^>]*>` also matches tags such as `<abbr>`, `<address>` or `<area>`, not only `<a ...>`. Those tags would be treated as anchors and compared against the English anchors, producing misleading \"Didn't find anchor tag\" errors. Require a word boundary, e.g. `</?a(\\s[^>]*)?>`."},
{"file": "misc/theme-verifier/src/main/java/org/keycloak/themeverifier/VerifyMessageProperties.java", "line": 79, "severity": "low", "category": "bug", "title": "Missing English bundle throws RuntimeException instead of a reported failure", "body": "If the derived English file does not exist, `verifySafeHtml` throws a bare RuntimeException. This happens for files without a locale suffix, or when the path regex derives the wrong name. The exception bypasses the `MojoExecutionException` handling in `verify()`, so the build fails with an unclear stack trace instead of a reported verification error. Throw a `MojoExecutionException`, or report the problem as a message."},
{"file": "misc/theme-verifier/src/test/java/org/keycloak/themeverifier/VerifyMessagePropertiesTest.java", "line": 33, "severity": "low", "category": "test_gap", "title": "No positive test and weakened duplicate-key assertion", "body": "Every test only checks that some error is reported. None verifies that a valid bundle, such as an allowed `<b>` in a translation whose English source also contains `<b>`, produces no messages, so false positives would go unnoticed. The duplicate-key assertion was also loosened from `contains` to `hasItem`, so unexpected extra errors for that fixture are no longer caught."}
]}
